XDJ-RX patch 14 -- drive the sub-ucom frame per SPI burst; room for full panel state.

1. The sub-ucom panel slave (fsl-imx6.c, patches 02/07/13) builds its 100-byte
   SubRxData frame -- operator holds, auto-level defaults, CRC-16/X-25 at [0x62] --
   in xdj_subucom_frame_start(), and rewinds its MISO position there. Nothing in
   the committed patch set ever CALLED it: the call lived only as an uncommitted
   edit in an old local build tree (docs/wip/subucom-inject-scaffolding.txt). A
   clean build therefore clocked out all-zero frames, rbp's reader saw an
   unchanging frame with a bad CRC, and no panel control (button, fader, jog,
   encoder) ever reached the firmware. Hook it at the start of every ECSPI burst
   in imx_spi_flush_txfifo() (weak, so imx_spi.c still links on its own).

2. MAXHOLD 20 -> 64: the virtual panel now sends its whole state every frame
   (every moved fader/knob, held buttons, jog + browse counters, input select).

3. Auto-level also centres both COLOR pots (0x2e/0x3e; 0 = filter fully on) and
   brings up CH2 (fader 0x3c, trim 0x36, EQ 0x34/0x38/0x3a) -- previously only
   CH1 was set, so deck 2 booted silent.

Firmware/kernel untouched -- QEMU-side only.

--- a/hw/ssi/imx_spi.c	2026-11-14 22:44:36
+++ b/hw/ssi/imx_spi.c	2026-11-14 22:44:36
@@ -166,6 +166,18 @@
 
     DPRINTF("Begin: TX Fifo Size = %d, RX Fifo Size = %d\n",
             fifo32_num_used(&s->tx_fifo), fifo32_num_used(&s->rx_fifo));
+
+    /*
+     * XDJ-RX: a new burst begins -- let the sub-ucom panel slave (fsl-imx6.c)
+     * rebuild its 100-byte frame (operator holds, auto-level, CRC) and rewind
+     * its MISO position. Weak so this file still links without the slave.
+     */
+    {
+        extern void __attribute__((weak)) xdj_subucom_frame_start(void);
+        if (xdj_subucom_frame_start) {
+            xdj_subucom_frame_start();
+        }
+    }
 
     while (!fifo32_is_empty(&s->tx_fifo)) {
         int tx_burst = 0;
